.TH MABOX-PERSISTENCE-USB 1 "2026-08-23" "mabox-persistence-usb @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mabox-persistence-usb \- write a mabox-snapshot ISO to a USB stick with a persistent overlay partition
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mabox-persistence-usb
.RI [ -h ]
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mabox-persistence-usb
writes a
.B mabox-snapshot
ISO to a removable USB disk, then appends one more partition \(em
.BR ext4 ,
labeled
.BR MABOX_PERSIST ,
sized to all remaining free space by default \(em for a writable overlay so
changes made while running from the stick survive a reboot.
.PP
Every
.B write
run wipes and rebuilds the whole target device unconditionally. There is no
mode that preserves an existing overlay across runs \(em re-running
.B write
is itself the reset/reclaim-space mechanism.
.PP
The boot-time mechanism that actually mounts
.B MABOX_PERSIST
as a writable overlay (an initramfs hook,
.IR miso_persist )
lives in the
.B mabox-snapshot
package, not this one, and is not implemented yet. Until it ships, a stick
written by this tool boots exactly like a plain mabox-snapshot ISO and the
persistence partition is present but unused \(em
.B write
prints an explicit warning about this every run.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS version
Print the installed version.
.SS doctor
Check prerequisites (required tools, currently-attached removable USB
disks). Read-only, no root needed.
.SS "devices list"
List currently-attached removable USB disks, with full identification
(size, vendor, model, serial, existing partitions). Read-only, no root
needed.
.SS "inspect ISO"
Validate an ISO before ever touching a device: ISO9660 volume-ID match,
filename convention, rootfs encryption status, checksum verification, and
persistence boot-hook support. Read-only, no root needed.
.SS "write ISO [options]"
Write ISO to a USB disk plus a
.B MABOX_PERSIST
overlay partition. Requires root.
.TP
.BR \-\-device " " \fIPATH\fR
Target disk explicitly (e.g.
.IR /dev/sdb )
instead of the interactive insert/detect flow. Still passes the full
removable-USB-only hard filter and both safety guards.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Non-interactive: skip the typed confirmation and the physical
unplug/replug re-verification. The removable-USB-only filter and both
safety guards always still apply.
.TP
.B \-\-force\-unmount
With
.BR \-\-yes ,
automatically unmount mounted partitions on the target instead of erroring.
.TP
.BR \-\-persist\-size " " \fISIZE\fR
Cap the
.B MABOX_PERSIST
partition instead of using all remaining space (e.g.
.IR 50GiB ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-persist
Write only the raw ISO bytes; skip creating
.B MABOX_PERSIST
entirely.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Bypass the ISO volume-ID soft check. Never bypasses the removable/USB
filter, the critical-mount guard, or the 2TiB size guard \(em those have
no override.
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-reinsert\-check
Interactive-mode-only: skip the physical unplug/replug re-verification
(e.g. when testing against a VM-attached virtual disk).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-verify
Skip the post-write verification pass.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Resolve the target device and print every command that would run; touch
nothing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Generic error, or the user aborted a confirmation.
.TP
.B 2
A hard safety filter or guard rejected the device (non-removable/non-USB
target, a critical mountpoint, or a device at/beyond the 2TiB MBR limit).
Never bypassable by any flag.
.TP
.B 3
The write completed but the post-write verification pass found a problem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mabox-snapshot (1)
